  "query_preview": "..\nFair conditions are expected across much of the Marianas through \nthis evening. Scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms are \nexpected to develop over Saipan and Tinian coastal waters late \ntonight as TD 31W barrels northwestward, with the current forecast \ntaking it north of Agrihan. However, 31W's motion, and position north\nof an attendant trade-wind trough, will drag a col area over the \nislands tonight, leading to light and gentle winds through at least \nearly Saturday morning. Winds will likely become light and variable \nat times. Tinian and Saipan are expected to see only the outermost \nrainbands associated with TD 31W, and these may end up somewhat \nlimited in coverage given its rapid northwest movement. Convection on\nthe far south-southwest periphery of 31W is currently moving into \nnortheastern Saipan coastal waters. For more information on TD 31W,\nsee the Tropical Systems section below.\n\nA fairly dry trade-wind regime looks to resume by Sunday morning, and\ncontinue through the coming week. Low-end scattered showers and\nisolated thunderstorms are possible from time to time with weak \ntransient trade-wind troughs, especially around Sunday night.",
